<!--
  Call-fixup for the unsigned 64-bit / 32-bit division runtime helper(s).
  Compiler RTL (MPC555 has no 64-bit hardware divide); folds the opaque call
  into a real '/' so callers read as (dividend) / (divisor).

  PPC EABI: args r3,r4,r5,r6 = dividend_hi, dividend_lo, divisor_hi, divisor_lo.
  The helper returns a 64-bit quotient in the r3:r4 pair; callers consume the
  low word (r4). We write ONLY r4 (the killed-by-call low word, not the EABI
  return register r3) so leaf callers don't inherit a spurious r3 return.
  Verified zero semantic drift across all caller sites (2026-06-03).
-->
<callfixup name="udiv64by32">
  <pcode>
    <body><![CDATA[
dvd:8 = (zext(r3) << 32) | zext(r4);
dvs:8 = (zext(r5) << 32) | zext(r6);
q:8 = dvd / dvs;
r4 = q:4;
    ]]></body>
  </pcode>
</callfixup>
